> In this PR, however, we are introducing a potentially expensive operation (set membership) into a performance critical section, rather than just reading a boolean.
> ...
> we may consider caching both the results of all plugins, and the results in particular of the SchedulingGates plugin.

So, (leaving the naming issue aside) is your core concern in this PR having `pInfo.UnschedulablePlugins.Has` in this shortcut path from a performance perspective? 

I'm not sure if we could see a visible throughput difference between `pInfo.UnschedulablePlugins.Has` (= O(1) map access [internally](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/fb7bbd2e5df36212ca5133bcbaa46dcdb4d18f0e/staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/sets/set.go#L78)) vs `pInfo.SchedulingGated` (= new field to cache a result of schedulinggate plugin).

With a new test case https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/125550, I checked the throughput in each case and didn't see a notable difference actually. (You can try on your machine too.)

